From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ae-automation-bot <ae-automation-bot@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 09:19:57 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 074/159] [ae-patch] Show when a session is working, quiet,
 waiting or scheduled

A session row showed a spinner only while its turn ran, so a session whose
turn had ended while agents, a background shell or a check-in were still
going looked finished, and a long silent step looked frozen.

Each session list row and websocket update now carries
background_task_count and active_child_count, from the server's existing
background-shell cache and the child ids the list already loads. The
sidebar adds three row states: waiting (a pulsing hourglass with the
count), quiet (an amber spinner once a running session has had no update
for five minutes) and scheduled (an alarm with the next check-in time).
Above the composer, a status line shows the elapsed time, the current step
and the last activity while working, the agents and shells still running
while waiting, and when a check-in will wake the session.
